// 🌐localized string
// nameId        Int
// name          DynamicLocalizedString @relation("BandRoleName", fields: [nameId], references: [id])
// descriptionId Int
// description   DynamicLocalizedString @relation("BandRoleDescription", fields: [descriptionId], references: [id])

// // 🟫softdelete
// isDeleted Boolean @default(false)

// // ®️recordkeeping
// createdAt       DateTime  @default(now())
// createdByUserId Int?
// createdByUser   User?     @relation("<name>", fields: [createdByUserId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)
// updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt
// updatedByUserId Int?
// updatedByUser   User?     @relation("<name>", fields: [updatedByUserId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

// // 👁️visibility:
// visiblePermissionId Int? // which permission determines visibility, when NULL, only visible by admins + creator
// visiblePermission   Permission? @relation("<name>", fields: [visiblePermissionId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)

// // Ⓜ️metadata (sort, color, icon)
// sortOrder Int @default(0)
// color        String? @db.VarChar(768)
// iconName     String? @db.VarChar(768)
//
//
//
// SIGNIFICANCE
// significance String?
// These values are used to attach behavior to things, like event statuses are
// user-configurable, but the system treats cancelled events differently than otherwise,
// so EventStatusSignificance.Cancelled exists.
//
// In general, avoid significance. They are useful as a kind of patch-point for experiments
// or introducing features without needing db migrations.
// But they are sometimes messy.
//
// Ideally use an enum (see enum SignInMethodType), but mostly we use a free string,
// because it's more flexible/extensible.

// NAMING / CASING
// types in PascalCase
// - enums
// - models
// fields in camelCase
// - column names (userId)
// - foreign objects (user)
// - foreign sets (userTagAssignments)
//
// foreign sets:
// - plural
// - descriptive and specific in the context of the model it belongs to
//   - good: `userTagsCreated` (on User), `bandName` (on DynamicLocalizedString)
//
// relation naming doesn't have a strict convention, but it should.
// - similar to foreign set naming, but specific also OUTSIDE of the model scope.
// - simplest rule is to concatenate the 2 foreign set field names (ish) with an underscore.
// - but may need adjustment so it's clear and unambiguous.
// - Both fields in singular form
//   - good: `UserTagAssignment_CreatedByUser` (on User + UserTagAssignment)
//   - good: `BandName_DynamicLocalizedString` (on UserTagAssignment)

